============================================================
  Section 2 — Rank Coordination and Barrier Synchronization
============================================================

  All ranks must reach a barrier before any rank proceeds.
  In production, a slow rank (network congestion, NUMA penalty,
  DataLoader stall) makes ALL ranks wait — this is why tensor
  parallelism requires balanced compute across all GPUs.

  We simulate this by having rank 0 do extra work before the barrier.

  [Standalone] Barrier semantics: in multi-process mode, all ranks
  must arrive before any proceeds. A slow rank stalls all others.

  ✓ Section 2 passed — barrier coordination demonstrated

============================================================
  Section 3 — Pipeline Bubble: Idle Time Quantification
============================================================

  Pipeline parallelism assigns transformer layers to stages.
  The pipeline bubble is the GPU idle fraction at startup/drain.

  Bubble fraction = (P - 1) / (M + P - 1)
  where P = pipeline stages, M = micro-batches per flush.

  Target: M > 4 * P to keep bubble below 20%.

     P     M    Bubble %  Notes
     4     1       75.0%  1 micro-batch — almost 75% idle!
     4     4       42.9%  4 micro-batches — 43% idle
     4    16       15.8%  16 micro-batches — 16% idle
     4    32        8.6%  32 micro-batches —  9% idle (production target)
     8    32       17.9%  8 stages, 32 micro-batches — 18% idle

  ✓ Section 3 passed — pipeline bubble formula verified

============================================================
  Section 4 — TP Compute vs Communication Crossover
============================================================

  For tensor parallelism to help (not hurt), compute time must exceed
  AllReduce communication time.

  AllReduce time  ≈ 2*(N-1)/N * bytes / bandwidth
  Compute time    ≈ 2 * B * S * H / (FLOP/s per GPU)

  The crossover batch size is where compute_time > allreduce_time.
  Below the crossover, tensor parallelism makes inference SLOWER.

  Llama-7B style layer: H=4096, S=512
  Backend                  BW (GB/s)   Crossover batch    TP=2 threshold
  NVLink 4 (H100)                900               0.2  ✓ TP helps
  NVLink 3 (A100)                600               0.3  ✓ TP helps
  InfiniBand HDR                  50               3.0  ✓ TP helps
  PCIe 4.0 x16                    32               4.8  ✓ TP helps

  Rule: Tensor parallelism is beneficial only when NVLink is available
  (crossover batch < 32). Over InfiniBand, TP hurts for small batches.

  ✓ Section 4 passed — TP compute/communication crossover verified

